12
00:40:19,199 --> 00:40:25,199
Seuss' The Grinch (or simply The Grinch) is a 2018 American animated
Christmas comedy film based on How the Grinch Stole Christmas!

13
00:43:40,799 --> 00:43:46,799
Produced by Illumination, it was directed by Scott Mosier and Yarrow
Cheney and written by Michael LeSieur and Tommy Swerdlow.

14
00:47:02,400 --> 00:47:08,400
Narrated by Pharrell Williams, the film stars Benedict Cumberbatch as the Grinch, with
Rashida Jones, Kenan Thompson, and Angela Lansbury in supporting roles.

15
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
The plot follows the Grinch, who plans to stop Whoville's Christmas celebration by
stealing all the town's decorations and gifts, with his pet dog Max.

16
00:53:45,599 --> 00:53:51,599
The film is the third screen adaptation of the book, following the
1966 television special and the 2000 live-action film.

17
00:57:07,199 --> 00:57:13,199
It was announced in 2013, and by 2016, Cumberbatch was cast, and
Cheney and Peter Candeland were set to direct.

18
01:00:28,799 --> 01:00:34,799
In 2018, Mosier took over Candeland's position as co-director.

19
01:03:50,400 --> 01:03:56,400
Danny Elfman composed the score, with a song written
and performed by Tyler, the Creator.

20
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The Grinch was released in the United States on November 9, 2018, by Universal.

21
01:10:33,599 --> 01:10:39,599
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $540 million, becoming the
highest-grossing Christmas film in history, as well as the highest-grossing Dr.

22
01:13:55,199 --> 01:14:01,199
Seuss film adaptation.

23
01:17:16,800 --> 01:17:22,800
The film explores themes of small town, holiday, author, christmas.

24
01:20:38,399 --> 01:20:44,399
The tone is emotional.
